Mercedes-Benz USA (MBUSA): Exfiltration of Legal Defense Infrastructure and PII (March 2026)

• Sophisticated data breach targeting the legal and warranty defense infrastructure of MBUSA, involving the exfiltration of 18.3 GB of sensitive litigation and customer records.[6, 7, 8, 9]
• Stolen data includes "every defensive strategy" for consumer warranty claims (Magnuson-Moss and Song-Beverly Acts), outside counsel billing rates, settlement policies, and "New Vendor Questionnaire" forms containing banking details.[6, 7, 9]
• Attributed to the threat actor "zestix," who posted the complete dataset for sale on a dark web forum for $5,000; the breach likely targeted a third-party legal vendor processing MBUSA data.[7, 8, 9]
• The incident presents significant litigation risk, as plaintiffs may gain access to defensive legal playbooks, and a high fraud risk due to the exposure of vendor banking information.[6, 9]
• While direct corporate system uptime was not impacted, the breach of 48 states' litigation data creates a long-term financial liability that could affect the group’s legal reserve requirements.[7, 9]
• This event underscores the critical systemic risk posed by the legal supply chain and the compromise of intellectual property related to corporate liability defense.[6, 9]
